00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:38,800
 So here is a picture of a fully relaxed sarcomere of a muscle fiber.

321
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:44,440
 We still have that appreciable H band where there are no thin filaments.

322
00:27:44,440 --> 00:27:48,400
 We just have that M line where the thick filaments will attach.

323
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:57,080
 So no thin filaments here, and we see that the Z disks are an appropriate length.

324
00:27:57,080 --> 00:28:03,400
 And we can see only a part of the thin filament, thin active filament partially overlaps the

325
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:04,400
 thick filament.

326
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:11,240
 However, when we go to a fully contracted sarcomere, we can see that this H band disappears because

327
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:15,280
 then the active filaments are being pulled towards that M line.

328
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:17,960
 So we no longer have that H band.

329
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:23,240
 We can see that the Z disks are being pulled closer together as well.

330
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:27,440
 However, notice how the A band length never changes.

331
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:29,440
 It still stays the same.

332
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:30,440
 Okay.

333
00:28:30,440 --> 00:28:35,480
 And we can see that the thin filament is being pulled towards that center of the sarcomere.

334
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:39,120
 So make sure you understand what occurs during contraction again.

