00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:19,820
 of the A band and provide for that elastic recoil when muscle contraction ends.

386
00:33:19,820 --> 00:33:26,680
 With regards to the innervation of the skeletal muscle, we have motor neurons that will innervate

387
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:30,120
 skeletal muscle tissue.

388
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:32,280
 We have structures within the motor neuron.

389
00:33:32,280 --> 00:33:34,720
 So for example, we have a neuromuscular junction.

390
00:33:34,720 --> 00:33:40,080
 This is the point where the nerve ending and the muscle fiber will meet.

391
00:33:40,080 --> 00:33:45,720
 In the neuromuscular junction, we have structures, which is basically the end of an axon of

392
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:50,480
 a neuron known as terminal buttons.

393
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:55,760
 So terminal butons are located at the ends of axons and store neurotransmitters.

394
00:33:55,760 --> 00:34:00,120
 And we'll learn about what neurotransmitters are, but basically neurotransmitters are sort

395
00:34:00,120 --> 00:34:10,040
 of like hormones that will help send the chemical signal from the neuron to the muscle.

396
00:34:10,040 --> 00:34:16,760
 So between the muscle fiber and the terminal butons at the neuromuscular junction, we have

397
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:19,960
 this space called the synaptic clef.

398
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:25,760
 The synaptic clef is the space between the axon terminal and the sarcolemma of the muscle

399
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:29,400
 fiber.

400
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:36,360
 So here we see the neuromuscular junction and the events that allow for stimulation to allow

401
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:40,880
 for muscle contraction to occur.

402
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:43,560
 So here are the events at the neuromuscular junction.

403
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:46,800
 So first we have a nerve impulse.

404
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:52,160
 This nerve impulse coming from the axon, it will stimulate the release of the neurotransmitter

405
00:34:52,160 --> 00:34:55,600
 acetylcholine into the synaptic clef.

406
00:34:55,600 --> 00:35:00,320
 So here we see the myelated axon, the motor neuron.

407
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:05,960
 Here we have our terminal butons that contain the neurotransmitter acetylcholine.

408
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:11,840
 So the electrical impulse will travel down the axon, the myelinated axon to the terminal

409
00:35:11,840 --> 00:35:19,760
 buton at the neuromuscular junction which will then release the neurotransmitter into

410
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:26,640
 the synaptic clef and from there the neurotransmitter will bind to receptors onto the sarcolemma.

411
00:35:26,640 --> 00:35:32,560
 So acetylcholine stimulates changes in the sarcolemma that excite the muscle fiber.

412
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:37,240
 So we have the release of calcium ions before that.

