00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:51,520
 So breaking down glycogen will help produce ATP which we use for energy.

435
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:57,120
 So we have oxidative fibers that produce ATP aeromically for these oxygen anaerobically

436
00:37:57,120 --> 00:38:05,280
 glycolytic fibers will produce ATP by glycolysis.

437
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:10,800
 So these skeletal muscle fibers will then be divided into three classes.

438
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:20,720
 We have our slow oxidative fibers again oxidative requiring oxygen to produce ATP aeromically

439
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:26,800
 and then example of our slow oxidative fibers are our red slow oxidative fibers.

440
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:29,440
 Then we have fast glycolytic fibers.

