00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:55,480
 oxygen rather produce ATP through anaerobic means via glycolysis.

445
00:38:55,480 --> 00:39:02,120
 So first we'll talk about our slow oxidative fibers these are our red fibers they're red

446
00:39:02,120 --> 00:39:09,160
 due to an abundant myoglobin they obtain energy from oxygen or aerobic metabolic reactions

447
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:16,160
 requiring oxygen they contain a large number of mitochondria and they are richly supplied

